\f2\b Chip is held back until the audience wants to know what the research is for.
\f1\b0  His warnings supply the answer: terrifying weapons and potentially catastrophic consequences. His naming Eloise appears to authenticate the whole preceding account, despite his testimony establishing no such connection.\
Finally, his detention explains why this supposedly remained secret. The Sages\'92 \'93off the board\'94 remarks and Eloise\'92s \'93Put him back\'94 and \'93Turn that camera off\'94 become evidence of deliberate suppression.\
The package\'92s conclusion is that 
\f2\b Alexander has uncovered his mother\'92s conspiracy and rescued its silenced witness
\f1\b0 . That is the claim his editing constructs; the gaps between those connections are where your viewers can recognise what has been done to the material.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

